---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { person } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this portfolio site handles your data: no cookies, no analytics, no forms. Only the email you choose to send."
  updated="9 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is the personal portfolio of {person.name}, a product designer based in {person.location}. This page explains what
    happens to your data when you visit the site or contact me.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The site has no cookies, no analytics, no tracking pixels and no forms.</li>
    <li>Fonts and images are served from the site itself, not from third-party services.</li>
    <li>I only receive your data if you choose to email me.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {person.name} is responsible for this site and for any data you send me. You can reach me at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site collects</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself collects nothing. It does not set cookies, does not use local storage to track you and does not
    include analytics or advertising scripts. The “Copy email” button copies my address to your clipboard on your
    device; nothing is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. When you open a page, GitHub may log technical data
    such as your IP address to keep the service secure and running. I do not have access to these logs. See the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>
    for details.
  </p>

  <h2>When you email me</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to me, I receive your email address, your name if you include it and whatever you write. I use this
    only to reply and to talk about work or a project with you. I do not sell or share it, and I do not add you to a
    mailing list. I keep the conversation for as long as it is relevant to our work and delete it when you ask me to.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to LinkedIn, Behance, Dribbble, GitHub and my CV. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and
    this policy does not cover them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask me what data I hold about you, and ask me to correct or delete it. Email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${person.email}`}>{person.email}</a> and I will reply as soon as I can. If you are in the European
    Union, you also have the rights given by the GDPR, including the right to complain to your local data protection
    authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, I will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</LegalPage>
